# Event_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Live-service or seasonal games (liveops_mobile).

## 2. This document owns
- Event structural patterns: entry conditions, duration rules, progression tracks, reward payout logic.
- Event archetypes (race/ladder/collection/co-op) and their repeat policies.
- Anti-frustration rules (catch-up, daily caps, pity equivalents for events).

## 3. This document does NOT own
- The live calendar (when events run) — LiveOps_Design.
- Event narrative themes — Bible / Script.
- Reward values — Resource / Monetization.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Event philosophy / 2. Archetypes / 3. Entry & gating / 4. Progression tracks / 5. Payout logic / 6. Catch-up rules / 7. Repeat & rerun policy / 8. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Event vs LiveOps: structure here, schedule there.
- Event rewards link to Resource; no inline economy numbers.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every track has a terminal reward and a fallback for partial completion.
- Rerun policy declared per archetype (fresh progress vs resume).
